#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147296 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147617 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35a19512-4ba7-59c1-ae00-7b8f158264fe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces"}] :question/id #uuid "0803c5b9-51e2-5d4e-9c8f-cd8d575a7bec" :question/math-academy-id "e-2760" :question/problem "What is the surface area of the triangular prism represented by the net below?\n\n![](images/da/dafb07440f60418465b579aad73119cd47d6def34ed0cf1229afc9affbb177e4.png)" :question/worked-solution "The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nAdding the areas, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 12+3\\times 48 \\\\  & =24+144 \\\\  & =168\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147298 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147618 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces: Word Problems"}] :question/id #uuid "c91d73c6-cb1f-55d2-986b-83f94a6a66ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-2762" :question/problem "Maggy is building a pyramid from a cardboard net, shown below.  What will be the total surface area of the pyramid?  \n\n![](images/29/29c918514e60da13363883770befd9d80098deaba0b45cfcafa3255feb143261.png)" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a triangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ triangular base and $3$ triangular sides.\n\nAdding the areas, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 10+3\\times 12 \\\\  & =10+36 \\\\  & =46\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147304 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147622 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given Some Lengths"}] :question/id #uuid "80466688-43e1-5697-976c-6ba63844fed9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2780" :question/problem "![](images/fe/fe43d65b35d583b21f25977a738e758a31d6b04eb08957877879cc54eef3f45f.png)\n\nBy assuming that all of the side faces have the same height $(8\\,\\text{in}),$ find the total surface area of the square pyramid above by considering its net." :question/worked-solution "The net of our pyramid is as follows:\n\n![](images/c4/c4a5fe995aaaf47b7ab2b90492059d739fc2352955dc1e12a71852fc13046a33.png)\n\nFirst, notice that the base of the pyramid is a square with sides equal to $5 \\, \\text{in}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of square} = 5 \\times 5 = 25 \\, \\text{in}^2.\n$$\n\n \n\nEach side face of our solid is triangle, where the base is $5\\,\\text{in}$ and the height is $8\\,\\text{in}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of triangle} = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 8 = 20 \\, \\text{in}^2.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the pyramid consists of $1$ square (the base) and $4$ triangles (the side faces). \n\nAdding the areas, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the square})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the triangle}) \\\\  & =1\\times 25+4\\times 20 \\\\  & =25+80 \\\\  & =105\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147907 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147617 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35a19512-4ba7-59c1-ae00-7b8f158264fe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e7002b1-4137-5822-b53e-011e127f2daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566456} {:answer/id #uuid "343befad-1c3c-5e44-8365-0ac2cf73b9f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566465} {:answer/id #uuid "55bb5eeb-01b4-563e-9c24-4b8067153a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566524} {:answer/id #uuid "c259ddf1-4a0f-5a4d-94b1-fa414462746d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566748} {:answer/id #uuid "e19f47e2-3b6a-5718-8c98-fcc5d0cd7c39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e19f47e2-3b6a-5718-8c98-fcc5d0cd7c39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566818} :answer-field/id #uuid "9865bd39-861c-546d-bc80-52ecf6dcce76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c68b4c0-9bb1-5498-b122-47cadbc90d21" :question/math-academy-id "q-61714" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0cb01fa25e07a0f18655c9b61b732ca0738ea6fbe735422f92925a7dcc6963be.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular prism represented by the net above?" :question/worked-solution "The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ squares (base and top) and $4$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 9+4\\times 12 \\\\  & =18+48 \\\\  & =66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147622 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given Some Lengths"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2802d72f-f544-5b69-9924-ce26c2923932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566449} {:answer/id #uuid "66284be8-1258-5a5f-b85d-cd5c1abb69c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "86\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566557} {:answer/id #uuid "8d9a1191-bd09-5e56-9d23-31da7071d93c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566634} {:answer/id #uuid "91a08974-22bf-5468-8a88-cbafb446715e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566650} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb191e3-8c09-5910-83d9-6d08306b5373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d9a1191-bd09-5e56-9d23-31da7071d93c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566634} :answer-field/id #uuid "58088e2e-469b-5686-99f3-b81f78e39d62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "530a5934-3144-5443-a3cd-8a236b03d6c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-61781" :question/problem "![](images/72/72450d407a3c4d043769ac1e331adc1625fd8d579e5f49409cfa718116e05581.png)\n\nNash paints a box that has the form of a rectangular prism. What is the total area that Nash needs to paint if the box is $6\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $3\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the net of our box.\n\n![](images/03/038c0ea6632481ee1eaece1637aac46b9a09389c0d363f4b3503b1944c039127.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $6\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=6\\times 3=18\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares have sides of length $3\\,\\text{cm}.$ Hence, the area of one square is\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=3\\times 3=9\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the bar consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 18+2\\times 9 \\\\  & =72+18 \\\\  & =90\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147622 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "947eb2bb-0443-5740-9d45-847c70877270" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given Some Lengths"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7d05a27-bc22-599f-9521-686cccb47526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392820} {:answer/id #uuid "b463f199-15d4-5666-95e5-3d376c7e7264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392821} {:answer/id #uuid "94740290-e368-5fc3-b155-957695497127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392822} {:answer/id #uuid "dda83309-31a3-50ae-8a59-56d809fefee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392823} {:answer/id #uuid "950ae5a7-059d-5882-b91e-7d6c0833c44d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dda83309-31a3-50ae-8a59-56d809fefee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392823} :answer-field/id #uuid "56ae08df-7b65-5143-b632-e7f82228c84e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17e99f21-4a32-5f31-9b6f-4f7bf7f5a533" :question/math-academy-id "q-62107" :question/problem "![](images/24/248ccfcbb3de8ab63622cfaf4c823ae1c1734742f5f8c9f14b1dfae0ff79eed2.png)\n\nWhat is the surface area of the box shown above knowing that  it is $4\\,\\text{m}$ long, $1\\,\\text{m}$ wide, and $1\\,\\text{m}$ tall?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the net of our box.\n\n \n\n![](images/c3/c35bb0f7b049baa569a06532b516436afaf310e28870cfbd4790467d36e54809.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $4\\,\\text{m}$ long and $1\\,\\text{m}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=4\\times 1=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $1\\,\\text{m}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=1\\times 1=1\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the box consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 4+2\\times 1 \\\\  & =16+2 \\\\  & =18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147617 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35a19512-4ba7-59c1-ae00-7b8f158264fe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c898171-26ce-5715-b0cf-aca25a35f36c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566421} {:answer/id #uuid "34a5c6ec-79a2-57f5-8e87-0619d5aa6204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "116\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566466} {:answer/id #uuid "603bf045-a13f-5c8c-bc67-7d6722164f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566546} {:answer/id #uuid "7613259f-b62a-5953-8040-3935f1e8b35d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "106\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566588} {:answer/id #uuid "b02a256b-6712-5fb1-8235-5ded51b4ecc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7613259f-b62a-5953-8040-3935f1e8b35d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "106\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566588} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c8d1d51-349d-5a36-98da-38f85155981a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37d91edf-acff-586d-ad14-90f9bbc2ae14" :question/math-academy-id "q-93260" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4ae8d09f2e4bca084d113aaa06f80570da8d628868ccd3c9c208337de303d068.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the triangular prism represented by the net above?" :question/worked-solution "The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 8+3\\times 30 \\\\  & =16+90 \\\\  & =106\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147618 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1636df6e-c36c-5694-809c-2595308f9d2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "274\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354868} {:answer/id #uuid "69be71f1-f11f-556a-b361-c708cd25bfdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "298\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355597} {:answer/id #uuid "bb726eac-67e6-52ae-b7ea-53cec9f6a137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "302\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356305} {:answer/id #uuid "e65f7cbf-75d5-5323-9333-18983c300cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "286\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356680} {:answer/id #uuid "f6da8cee-ac77-5205-b7d1-0164d6c5c262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "264\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69be71f1-f11f-556a-b361-c708cd25bfdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "298\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355597} :answer-field/id #uuid "96f21fe4-6d0d-55f7-b1c7-8628d5f0c001" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7e0efa5-6423-5a61-a04b-01649c479f66" :question/math-academy-id "q-93339" :question/problem "![](images/a6/a60731e7df54bb8f18f834b818c3e49c79fb30e67f7ed50c40f40aa813689ece.png)\n\nA manufacturer produces an unfair tetrahedral die from a plastic net, shown above. What is the total surface area of the die?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a triangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ base triangle and $3$ side triangles. \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 64+3\\times 78 \\\\  & =64+234 \\\\  & =298\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147618 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1233be4b-7634-5882-9ae5-3200a9da71d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Surface Area of a Polyhedron Given the Areas of the Faces: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b40c4dd3-1d79-54b0-823b-dbcec9da032f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394869} {:answer/id #uuid "56beaf5c-1cdd-555a-929d-05414265748d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394870} {:answer/id #uuid "cec913c6-692b-55f2-a18c-269be0d2cbc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394871} {:answer/id #uuid "242e6691-583b-5dcd-9ea4-1ea760a5e7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394872} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3041e7-9b3f-53a2-9125-16a47ceb3ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "242e6691-583b-5dcd-9ea4-1ea760a5e7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394872} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5dd29b7-7c45-5120-8f4f-b750b0c0e6da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d119284d-a155-58d7-994e-d134bc9c1879" :question/math-academy-id "q-93343" :question/problem "![](images/3d/3d0b6b63883b58ecce92e395380b140b32946a4bb037e1829544539749412af9.png)\n\nLiz deconstructs a lantern and gets the net shown above. In the figure, the areas of two of its faces are shown. What is the total surface area of the lantern?" :question/worked-solution "The net shown corresponds to a triangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ triangle (base) and $3$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 5+3\\times 13 \\\\  & =5+39 \\\\  & =44\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
